//! The voxel package: worlds of voxels drawn by walking rays through
//! them, as functions any Kernel calls. A ray walks a volume voxel by
//! voxel to the first that is not empty; a box of voxels placed in the
//! world, turned about its up axis, is met by the same walk carried into
//! its frame, so a still world and the bodies moving in it are drawn
//! alike; what a ray meets is lit by the sky and a sun, or by lights that
//! fade with distance, kept to a few steps as pixel art keeps them, and
//! fades into fog or the dark. There are no Kernels here, only the
//! arithmetic they share.
package voxel@1 { language = 1; ir = 1; }

use "kernels/";
